          "type": "turn",
          "question": "my poo has been really dark, almost black and sticky, for three days and I feel light headed when i stand",
          "answer": "**Get emergency care now. Call your local emergency number, or go to the nearest emergency department. Do not wait to see if it passes.**\n\nBlack, sticky stools together with feeling light-headed when you stand can be a sign of bleeding higher up in the digestive tract. The gastrointestinal bleeding guidance says that blood from the stomach or upper bowel \"arrives black and tarry\" and that this kind of bleeding \"frequently accompanies a larger volume of loss than the appearance suggests.\" The acute abdominal pain guidance lists \"black tarry stools\" with \"dizziness\" among the situations to call emergency services for immediately.\n\nThe urgency check returned \"routine\" because none of its fixed rules matched your description. That is a gap in the rule table, not a clearance. The guidance I found says the safer assumption is bleeding until a clinician has assessed it. Iron tablets or bismuth medicines can also darken stool, but do not assume that is the cause. Only someone examining you can tell.\n\nWhile you wait for help, sit or lie down, and avoid standing up quickly. If you faint, become confused, vomit blood or material that looks like coffee grounds, or feel chest pain or breathlessness, tell the emergency team straight away.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
